# Regenerating the SDK

Everything in `src` and the `build.zig`, `.gitattributes` and `docs/REGENERATING.md` files are generated by [openapi2zig](https://github.com/christianhelle/openapi2zig) from `{{spec}}`, using the settings in `openapi2zig.json`. Don't edit them by hand, because regenerating overwrites them.

Files written only once and then owned by you (`README.md`, `LICENSE`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `build.zig.zon`, `.gitignore`, `docs/USAGE.md`, the CI workflows and the examples) are never touched unless you pass `--force`.

The current SDK was generated with openapi2zig {{generator_version}}. Each generated Zig file records its generator version in its header.

## Install openapi2zig

Linux/macOS:

```bash
curl -fsSL https://christianhelle.com/openapi2zig/install | bash
```

Windows (PowerShell Core):

```powershell
irm https://christianhelle.com/openapi2zig/install.ps1 | iex
```

## Generate

Run this from the root of the repository:

```bash
openapi2zig generate --sdk
```

The generator skips a file when only its header would change. Pass `--force` to rewrite everything.

## After generating

1. Run `zig build test`, `zig build check` and `zig build examples`.
2. Update the known limitations in [USAGE.md](USAGE.md) if anything changed.
3. Update the generator version in this file, the README and the changelog.
